{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22443 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Yahazuno is implicated in the biological activity of VMRC-MELG through a series of molecular interactions that involve the MIP (Molecular Interaction Platform) as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that Ent-Yahazuno directly targets MIP, which in turn is the target of multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and 5,7-Dihydroxy-6-methyl-2-nonacosylchromone. These compounds, in turn, target VMRC-MELG, indicating a cascade of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the interaction between Ent-Yahazuno and VMRC-MELG. The consistent presence of MIP as a common target across these pathways suggests a potential mechanism where Ent-Yahazuno modulates the activity of MIP, which then influences VMRC-MELG. This integrated pathway highlights the importance of MIP in mediating the effects of Ent-Yahazuno, and the evidence supports a role for Ent-Yahazuno in regulating the activity of VMRC-MELG through this intermediary.",
